r  zorro at the start  of course soros fight played an  important part here  but i think that luffy being a conqueror  hockey user  probably already radiated a strong sense  of will  and it is probably also at this moment  here that mihawk remembers the story  that shanks told him of how he lost his  arm  seeing luffy's powers and the straw hats  i think we can  even see this moment of recognition in  this panel here  where luffy first stretches his arm but  i think the dialogue does even more here  though  as especially in the japanese but also  in the english version  the words that mihawk uses to address  sorrow more and more reflect his change  in attitude  and his rising level of respect for him  his speech pattern switches from this  by his first name and challenges him to  surpass him  i think to some degree this is due to  mihawk yearning for a true challenge  after losing shanks  but i also believe that as a master  swordsman and sharing zoro's values and  beliefs  he has chosen zorro as worthy to follow  in his footsteps  and keep these values alive and defend  their craft against non-believers  if you want to bring it back to the  religious theme  and so i believe it makes for an even  starker contrast when mihawk is finally  approached by don creek again  as his face completely reverts from an  excited glow  to disgust and annoyance and he slashes  the ship once more  before disappearing because i feel with  this  he contrasts the difference between  luffy and creek before their battle even  begins  now last but not least i of course want  to address zoro's speech to luffy  which is the second of my favorite zorro  moments in the scene  after luffy has displayed true care and  fear for his first mate's life  even shedding a rare tear zaro now  publicly acknowledges and honors luffy  for the very first time in the story  zorro clearly has realized luffy's true  love and respect for him  as he apologizes for worrying his  captain he declares that he will n